* Korg MS-10 VCF: IC16 KORG35 plus its external parts, from the service manual circuit diagram.
* External parts (real values): R57 12k / R59 47R input attenuator (R56 4k7 to the EXT level amp),
*   C12 3.3n (floating, to the peak-feedback node), C13 1n (to ground),
*   peak amp IC7 (1/2 4558): R64 270k || D10,D11 (1S1588), R63 4k7 + C16 10u to ground,
*   C19 33u -> R62 2k2 -> VR13 10kB PEAK pot -> R61 5k6 || C15 1n -> feedback node, R60 220R to ground.
* KORG35 internals are NOT in the manual. Assumed here: two BJT differential-pair transconductors
*   (the Sallen-Key "resistors"), a matched-pair exponential converter, unity output buffer on pin 7.

.model npnx NPN(IS=1e-14 BF=200)
.model d1s1588 D(IS=2.52e-9 N=1.752)

* BJT differential-pair OTA. Iout (into node out) = alpha*Itail*tanh((Vp-Vn)/(2*VT))
.subckt ota inp inn out tail vcc
Q1 c1 inp tail npnx
Q2 c2 inn tail npnx
Vs1 vcc c1 0
Vs2 vcc c2 0
F1 0 out Vs1 1
F2 out 0 Vs2 1
.ends ota

* Matched-pair exponential converter, two outputs. Ic(out) = Iref * exp(Vc/VT)
.subckt expo vc tailA tailB params: iref=1u
Vbref bref 0 -2
Iref 0 c1x DC {iref}
Qe1 c1x bref eme npnx
Eop eme 0 0 c1x 1e5
Ebc bc bref vc 0 1
Qa tailA bc eme npnx
Qb tailB bc eme npnx
.ends expo

* in: VCO signal (volts) at R57.  out: KORG35 pin 7.  vc: expo control voltage.  peak: 0..1 (VR13 rotation)
.subckt ms10vcf in out vc vcc params: iref=1u peak=0.5
R57 in n7 12k
R56 n7 0 4.7k
R59 n7 0 47
X1 n7 v1 v1 tailA vcc ota
C12 v1 f 3.3n
X2 v1 v2 v2 tailB vcc ota
C13 v2 0 1n
Xe vc tailA tailB expo iref={iref}
E7 out 0 v2 0 1
* IC7 peak amp
Eamp a 0 out nm 1e6
R64 nm a 270k
D10 a nm d1s1588
D11 nm a d1s1588
R63 nm c16 4.7k
C16 c16 0 10u
C19 a b 33u
R62 b t 2.2k
Ra t w {(1-peak)*10k + 0.01}
Rb w 0 {peak*10k + 0.01}
R61 w f 5.6k
C15 w f 1n
R60 f 0 220
.ends ms10vcf
